PART 4: PUBLIC MEMBERSHIP VERIFICATION SYSTEM

Build a prominent, independent and fully functional membership verification portal.

This feature must be accessible without requiring the visitor to create an account.

Page title:

"VERIFY A DIGITAL BODA MEMBER"

Supporting text:

"Confirm the membership status and identity of an individual claiming to represent the Digital Boda Drivers and Deliveries Association of Kenya."

4.1 Verification Methods

Provide three verification methods:

Method A: Membership Number

Allow visitors to enter a unique membership number.

Method B: QR Code

Allow visitors to scan the QR code on the member's digital membership card.

Method C: National ID Verification

Allow an authorized verification workflow using an applicant's national ID number, subject to appropriate privacy safeguards.

Do not publicly expose national ID numbers or allow unrestricted searches using sensitive personal identifiers.

4.2 Verification Results

When a valid membership number or QR code is submitted, retrieve the member's record from the database.

Display:

- Member's photograph, where consent permits.
- Full name.
- Membership number.
- Membership category.
- County or operating region.
- Membership status.
- Verification date.
- Official association branding.
- Secure verification reference.

Possible membership statuses:

- VERIFIED / ACTIVE.
- PENDING APPROVAL.
- EXPIRED.
- SUSPENDED.
- INACTIVE.
- REVOKED.
- NOT FOUND.

Use clear visual status indicators.

A successful verification must mean the member is currently approved and in good standing according to the association's configured membership rules.

If a record is suspended, expired or revoked, clearly communicate that it is not currently valid.

Never display sensitive personal information, residential addresses, full national ID numbers or private contact information.

4.3 Anti-Fraud and Security

Implement:

- Cryptographically secure verification tokens.
- Non-guessable membership identifiers.
- QR-code validation against the live database.
- Rate limiting.
- CAPTCHA or equivalent abuse protection.
- Audit logs.
- Protection against fabricated membership cards.
- Revocation of compromised cards.
- Detection of duplicate membership records.

A downloaded or printed card must not be treated as proof of active membership without live verification.

